//
// GEMMA4-E2B Q4NX prefill TTFT vs padded prefill length, into
// gemma4_e2b_q4nx.prefill_sweep.json (collected by the nightly LLM benchmark).
//
// The axis is the PADDED length, not the prompt length: this prefill pads the
// prompt to the length its ELFs were BUILT for and reads the last real token's
// row, so at a fixed engine TTFT does not move with the prompt. Every point
// here therefore rebuilds all 22 ELFs, and sweep_prefill.py fails the point
// rather than reporting a number if they came out at some other length.
//
// The counterpart to run_npu2_sweep.lit (decode tok/s vs KV depth). They cannot
// share a table: one is latency against problem size, the other throughput
// against cache depth.
//
// Lengths stop at 2048. That is the largest this example has been RUN at, and
// it is the length the correctness gate (run_npu2_verify_prefill.lit) scores;
// adding 4096 without measuring it first would publish a number from a build
// nothing has validated.
//
// Latency only, never a correctness gate. The per-length first-token argmax the
// driver prints is recorded with each point because a bad build shows up there
// first -- but a missed argmax does NOT fail the point, since the driver only
// turns that into an exit status under --gate.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano, peano_ge22, hfweights_fastflowlm_gemma4_e2b_it_npu2
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_peano_prefill_sweep
// RUN: cd test_peano_prefill_sweep
// RUN: %PYTHON %S/../bench/sweep_prefill.py --model-name gemma4_e2b_q4nx --makefile %S/Makefile --lengths 512,1024,2048 --peano-dir %PEANO_INSTALL_DIR --out gemma4_e2b_q4nx.prefill_sweep.json
// RUN: FileCheck %s < gemma4_e2b_q4nx.prefill_sweep.json
// CHECK: "model": "gemma4_e2b_q4nx"
// CHECK: "axis": "prefill_len"
// A parsed number at the reference length, not just a well-formed file: if the
// driver's TTFT line drifts out of sweep_prefill.py's regex every point goes
// null and the published curve silently empties while the test stays green.
// CHECK: "prefill_len": 2048
// CHECK-NEXT: "ttft_ms": {{[0-9]}}
